### Chart title
Do NOT add titles as HTML — they won't be part of the chart or exports. Use `am5.Label` in the container BEFORE the chart, with `verticalLayout`:
```js
root.container.children.push(am5.Label.new(root, {
  text: "Chart Title",
  fontSize: "1.3em",
  x: am5.p50,
  centerX: am5.p50
}));
root.container.set("layout", root.verticalLayout);

var chart = root.container.children.push(am5xy.XYChart.new(root, { ... }));
```

## Key differences from amCharts 4 (common AI mistakes)

| amCharts 4 (WRONG) | amCharts 5 (CORRECT) |
|---------------------|----------------------|
| `am4core.create("div", am4charts.XYChart)` | `am5.Root.new("div")` then `am5xy.XYChart.new(root, {})` |
| `new am4charts.CategoryAxis()` | `am5xy.CategoryAxis.new(root, { ... })` |
| `chart.data = [...]` | `series.data.setAll([...])` |
| `series.dataFields.valueY = "v"` | `valueYField: "v"` in `.new()` settings |
| `am4core.color("#f00")` | `am5.color(0xff0000)` or `am5.color("#f00")` |
| `new am4charts.Legend()` | `am5.Legend.new(root, {})` |
| `chart.cursor = new am4charts.XYCursor()` | `chart.set("cursor", am5xy.XYCursor.new(root, {}))` |
| SVG-based rendering | Canvas by default; SVG optional since 5.21.0 (`renderer: am5.SVGRenderer`) |
| `am4core.useTheme(am4themes_animated)` | `root.setThemes([am5themes_Animated.new(root)])` |

## Common pitfalls

1. **CategoryAxis needs data too** — Unlike ValueAxis, CategoryAxis must receive data: `xAxis.data.setAll(data)` in addition to `series.data.setAll(data)`.

2. **Date values must be timestamps** — DateAxis expects numbers (ms since epoch), not Date objects or strings. Use `new Date(...).getTime()`.

3. **Renderer is required for every axis** — Always pass a `renderer` when creating an axis: `am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {})`.

4. **Don't forget `root` in `.new()` calls** — Every `.new()` call (except Root itself) takes `root` as the first arg.

5. **Dispose via root** — To clean up, call `root.dispose()`, not `chart.dispose()`.

6. **Colors** — Use `am5.color(0xFF0000)` or `am5.color("#ff0000")`. For color sets, access `chart.get("colors")`.

7. **Percent values** — Use `am5.percent(50)` not plain `50` or `"50%"` when a setting expects a Percent value.

8. **children.push()** — Adding elements to containers uses `.children.push()` which returns the element. Always capture the return value.

9. **No CSS styling** — amCharts 5 draws on canvas by default, so CSS cannot reach chart elements; even with `am5.SVGRenderer` (5.21.0) the shapes have no per-element classes, are rewritten on redraw, and exports ignore page CSS. Use themes or `.set()`/`.setAll()`.

10. **Hierarchy charts are chart-less** — Treemap, force-directed, etc. add series directly to `root.container` (or a wrapper Container), not to a chart object.

11. **`dataItems` is a plain array** — `series.dataItems` does NOT have `.each()`. Use `series.dataItems.forEach(fn)` or `am5.array.each(series.dataItems, fn)`. Only `series.data` (the ListData object) has `.each()`.

12. **CDN script load order matters** — `index.js` must load first, then `xy.js`, then any package that depends on it (`radar.js`, `timeline.js`, `gantt.js`). Wrong order causes runtime errors. Correct order: `index.js` > `xy.js` > `radar.js` / `timeline.js` / `gantt.js` > `themes/*.js`.

13. **No `minorGrid` / `minorTicks` / `minorLabels` objects** — These properties don't exist. Enable minor grid via renderer flags:
```js
am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {
  minorGridEnabled: true,    // shows minor grid lines
  minorLabelsEnabled: true   // optional: shows minor labels
})
```
Style minor elements through theme rules targeting the `"minor"` tag — they auto-inherit main grid appearance but slightly lighter.

14. **Flow chart animated bullets go on `series.bullets`, NOT `series.links.template.bullets`** — To animate labels/circles flowing along Sankey/Chord links, use `series.bullets.push()`. Animate `bullet.locationX` (Sankey) or `bullet.locationY` (Chord) from 0>1 with `loops: Infinity`. Use an adapter on opacity based on position for fade effect:
```js
// Sankey: use locationX. For Chord: replace ALL locationX with locationY.
series.bullets.push(function(root, series, dataItem) {
  var label = am5.Label.new(root, {
    text: "${value}B", populateText: true,
    centerX: am5.p50, fill: am5.color(0xffffff)
  });
  var bullet = am5.Bullet.new(root, {
    locationX: 0, sprite: label, autoRotate: true
  });
  bullet.animate({
    key: "locationX", from: 0, to: 1,
    duration: Math.random() * 10000 + 2000, loops: Infinity
  });
  label.adapters.add("opacity", function(opacity) {
    return 0.5 - Math.abs(0.5 - bullet.get("locationX"));
  });
  bullet.on("locationX", function() {
    label.set("opacity", label.get("opacity"));
  });
  return bullet;
});
```

15. **`MapPointSeries` needs `latitudeField`/`longitudeField` unless your data fields are named exactly `latitude`/`longitude`** — Since 5.16.1 those are the defaults, so matching data works undeclared. Any other naming silently renders nothing:
```js
// FINE since 5.16.1 — data uses "latitude"/"longitude", which are the defaults
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {})

// WRONG — data uses lat/lng, points won't show
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {})

// CORRECT — tell the series which fields hold coordinates
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {
  latitudeField: "lat",
  longitudeField: "lng"
})
```
Neither is needed when using `pushDataItem({ latitude: ..., longitude: ... })`, which passes coordinates directly to the data item. On amCharts older than 5.16.1 there were no defaults — declare both fields explicitly if you need to support those versions.

16. **`data.setAll()` does NOT animate — use `data.setIndex()` for animated updates** — `series.data.setAll(newData)` replaces everything instantly with no transition. To update data with smooth animation, use `series.data.setIndex(i, newItem)` per item:
```js
// WRONG — no animation
series.data.setAll(newData);

// CORRECT — animates each value change
newData.forEach(function(item, i) {
  series.data.setIndex(i, item);
});
```

17. **`color.lighten()` / `color.darken()` are NOT instance methods** — `am5.color(0xff0000).lighten(0.3)` does NOT work. Use static methods: `am5.Color.lighten(color, 0.3)` to lighten, `am5.Color.lighten(color, -0.3)` to darken. There is NO `darken()` method — use negative lighten. Also: `am5.Color.brighten()`, `am5.Color.saturate()`.

18. **Venn diagram has no `VennDiagram` class** — `am5venn.Venn` is pushed directly into a `Container`, NOT into a chart's `series`. See references/venn.md.

19. **Timeline `AxisRendererCurveX` requires `yRenderer`** — Always create the Y renderer first, then pass it:
```js
var yRenderer = am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveY.new(root, {});
var xRenderer = am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveX.new(root, {
  yRenderer: yRenderer
});
```
Without this, crashes with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'axis')`.

20. **Gantt data uses TWO separate calls** — Do NOT use `chart.data.setAll()`. Set categories on `chart.yAxis.data.setAll([{id, name, parentId, color}])` and tasks on `chart.series.data.setAll([{id, start, duration, progress, linkTo}])`. Use flat `parentId` for hierarchy, NOT nested `children` arrays. CDN order: `index.js` > `xy.js` > `plugins/colorPicker.js` > `gantt.js` > `themes/Animated.js`:
```js
// WRONG — single data call with nested children
chart.data.setAll([{ name: "Task", children: [...] }]);

// CORRECT — two separate calls with flat parentId hierarchy
chart.yAxis.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", name: "Phase 1", color: am5.color(0x297373) },
  { id: "task1", name: "Task 1", parentId: "phase1" }
]);
chart.series.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", start: timestamp, duration: 10, progress: 50 },
  { id: "task1", start: timestamp, duration: 5, progress: 100, linkTo: ["phase1"] }
]);
```

21. **No continent-level geodata at top-level CDN** — `geodata/europeLow.js` does NOT exist. Use `geodata/region/world/europeLow.js` (global: `am5geodata_region_world_europeLow`) or filter `worldLow` with `include: ["FR", "DE", "ES", ...]`.

22. **Do not add chart titles as HTML** — HTML titles are outside the chart and won't appear in exports. Use `am5.Label` pushed into the container BEFORE the chart, with `verticalLayout` on the container. See "Chart title" in Common components above.

23. **`XYChartScrollbar` axes — never use `scrollbar.get("xAxis")`** — Axes passed to the scrollbar constructor are NOT stored as gettable settings. Create axes as separate variables, pass them to the scrollbar, and reuse those same variables for the scrollbar's inner series:
```js
// WRONG — scrollbar.get("xAxis") returns undefined
var sbSeries = scrollbar.chart.series.push(am5xy.LineSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: scrollbar.get("xAxis"),   // undefined!
  yAxis: scrollbar.get("yAxis")    // undefined!
}));

// CORRECT — reuse the axis variables
var sbxAxis = am5xy.DateAxis.new(root, { renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {}) });
var sbyAxis = am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, { renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererY.new(root, {}) });
var scrollbar = am5xy.XYChartScrollbar.new(root, { xAxis: sbxAxis, yAxis: sbyAxis });
var sbSeries = scrollbar.chart.series.push(am5xy.LineSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: sbxAxis, yAxis: sbyAxis, valueYField: "value", valueXField: "date"
}));
```

24. **`am5.color()` only accepts hex integers or CSS strings** — `am5.color(0xff0000)`, `am5.color("#ff0000")`, `am5.color("rgb(255,0,0)")` are valid. `am5.color({ r: 255, g: 0, b: 0 })` is NOT — it throws.

25. **`MapChart` has NO `"colors"` setting** — `chart.get("colors")` returns `undefined` on `MapChart`. Only XY, Radar, and Percent charts auto-create a ColorSet. For maps, create your own: `am5.ColorSet.new(root, {})`.

26. **`VoronoiTreemap` has NO `.rectangles` property** — Unlike `Treemap` (which has `series.rectangles.template`), `VoronoiTreemap` renders organic polygon cells. Style via `series.nodes.template` and its children, not `.rectangles`.
27. **Labels with data placeholders need `populateText: true`** — When a Label uses data field placeholders like `text: "{name}"`, you MUST also set `populateText: true`. Without it, the placeholder is not resolved and the label appears blank. This applies everywhere Labels display dynamic data — bullet labels, map point labels, etc. Example: `am5.Label.new(root, { text: "{name}", populateText: true, ... })`.
28. **Globe rotation uses negative coordinates** — To center the globe (`geoOrthographic`) on a geographic point, set `rotationX` to **-longitude** and `rotationY` to **-latitude**. E.g., to center on Paris (48.86°N, 2.35°E): `chart.animate({ key: "rotationX", to: -2.35 }); chart.animate({ key: "rotationY", to: -48.86 });`. Using positive values rotates the globe the wrong way.
29. **`positionOnLine` with multi-segment lines limits per-segment control** — `MapPointSeries` data items can animate along a line via `positionOnLine` (0>1). If the line has 3+ points (multi-segment), position 0.5 is the midpoint of the *entire* path, making per-segment effects (scaling at each segment midpoint, pausing between segments, etc.) difficult. For advanced per-segment animations, use **single-segment lines** (2 points each) and animate the bullet across them sequentially. Since 5.20.6 a point on a line can be a plain data row — `{ lineId: "jfk-lhr", positionOnLine: 0, autoRotate: true }` (the line's data `id`) — instead of `pushDataItem({ lineDataItem })`; data rows are serialized, pushed data items are not. A looping flight can be declared on the bullet sprite: `animations: [{ target: "dataItem", key: "positionOnLine", from: 0, to: 1, duration: 6000, loops: 0, yoyo: true }]` (5.20.8) — with `autoRotate` the point then turns round on the way back (a point moved by `dataItem.animate()` in code is not flipped).
30. **`MapSankeySeries` is in the map package, NOT the flow package** — Geographic Sankey bands on a map use `am5map.MapSankeySeries` from `@amcharts/amcharts5/map`. Do NOT import `@amcharts/amcharts5/flow` for this. It requires a `polygonSeries` setting pointing to a `MapPolygonSeries` to resolve country IDs to centroids. Data uses `{ sourceId, targetId, value }` with ISO alpha-2 country codes. Bands are styled via `sankeySeries.mapPolygons.template`, nodes via `sankeySeries.nodes.mapPolygons.template`. Supports waypoints, explicit lat/long coordinates, multi-level flows, and animated bullets via `locationX`. Data can be set directly (e.g. `sankeySeries.data.setAll([...])`) at any time — `MapSankeySeries` auto-resolves `sourceId`/`targetId` once the referenced `polygonSeries` finishes loading, so no `datavalidated` wrapper is needed. **Never** call `polygonSeries.data.setAll()` with custom objects — this replaces geoJSON-derived data items and breaks centroid resolution.

31. **Do NOT exclude Antarctica (`exclude: ["AQ"]`) by default** — Many amCharts demos exclude Antarctica because they use Mercator projection where it appears disproportionately large. This is a demo-specific choice, not a best practice. Unless the user explicitly asks to exclude Antarctica, or references a demo that does so, keep Antarctica in the map. With non-Mercator projections (`geoNaturalEarth1`, `geoEqualEarth`, `geoOrthographic`, `geoEquirectangular`), Antarctica renders at a reasonable size.

32. **Custom GeoJSON for `MapPolygonSeries` needs CLOCKWISE exterior rings** — the RFC 7946 counter-clockwise default is read by the spherical projection as "the globe minus the polygon", so every polygon floods the whole map. amCharts does not rewind; reverse each ring: `g.coordinates = g.coordinates.map(ring => ring.slice().reverse())`. To fit a custom region use `chart.zoomToGeoBounds({ left, right, top, bottom }, duration)` (left/right = longitude, top/bottom = latitude).

33. **`axis.dispose()` does NOT remove the axis from `chart.xAxes`/`yAxes`** — use `chart.yAxes.removeValue(axis)` / `removeIndex(i)` (the list disposes it). `series.dispose()` does self-remove from `chart.series`; axes are the exception.

34. **Declare bullet callbacks as `function(root, series, dataItem)`** — closing over an outer `root` breaks JSON round-trips through `ChartSerializer`. A `ColorSet` must always contain ≥1 color (`set("colors", [])` crashes `next()`); swap in a fresh `am5.ColorSet.new(root, {})` instead.

35. **Tooltips on non-XY charts need no `am5.Tooltip` instance** — just `tooltipText` on the right template (`slices.template`, `nodes.template`, flow `nodes.nodes.template` / `links.template`, wordcloud `labels.template`, `mapPolygons.template`); the root's shared tooltip (`root.container.get("tooltip")`) is used. Create a `Tooltip` only when it must look different, or on XY charts where series/axis tooltips are cursor-driven. Heat rules on bullets: `target` must be the `am5.Template` the sprite is built from, `dataField` is the property key (`"valueY"`, not the column name), and `calculateAggregates: true` is required — otherwise every bullet silently gets the same size.

36. **Serialize the chart's top container child** (`serializer.serializeAll(root.container.children.getIndex(0))` — the chart, or the series on chart-less types). Before 5.21.0 a series straight in `root.container` or one with `selectedDataItem` set overflowed the stack; 5.21.0 handles both (a drilled-down hierarchy selection is still not restored). `ChartSerializer` does not capture adapters, Venn `hoverGraphics`, a `ZoomTools` you added to a hand-made `ZoomableContainer` (use `am5.SerialChartContainer`), or data items added with `pushDataItem()` — re-apply those after `JsonParser.parse()`. It does save user `themeTags` (5.20.6), declared `animations`, endless code-started loops (`loops: Infinity`, named easing) as `animations` entries (5.20.8, `runningAnimations`, default `true`), and since 5.21.0 a data-item loop started in code (the first one found, onto the bullet sprite), hidden series, elements added to plot/axis containers, a `ZoomableContainer`'s `contents`, `Date` values, and `root.interfaceColors` colors as `"@root.interfaceColors.get('…')"` references. Prefer a declared `animations` entry over `animate()` for effects that must survive JSON; for the opening animation use `autoAppear: true` (5.21.0).

## Disposal (SPA / React / Angular / Vue)

**Always call `root.dispose()`** — this cleans up all children, series, and event listeners.

```js
// React
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  const root = am5.Root.new("chartdiv");
  // ... build chart
  return () => { root.dispose(); };
}, []);

// Angular
ngOnDestroy() { this.root?.dispose(); }

// Vue
onUnmounted(() => { root.dispose(); });
```

## Recent API changes (5.16 → 5.21.0)

**Renamed settings** (old name still works but is deprecated):

| Class(es) | Old | New | Since |
|-----------|-----|-----|-------|
| `MovingAverage`, `MovingAverageDeviation`, `MovingAverageEnvelope`, `BollingerBands` | `type` | `maType` | 5.18.0 |
| `VoronoiTreemap` | `type` | `shapeType` | 5.18.0 |

**Breaking — WordCloud (5.20.1):** layout is now computed synchronously in one pass. The per-data-item `ghostLabel` is gone and labels live in an internal container — use `series.labels` / `dataItem.get("label")` instead of walking `series.children`.

**New in 5.21.0 (2026-10-08):**

- SVG rendering: `am5.Root.new("chartdiv", { renderer: am5.SVGRenderer })` (only when the root is created) or `am5.Root.defaultRenderer = am5.SVGRenderer` before creating roots. Canvas stays the default; charts look and behave the same; blend modes `DST_OVER`/`SRC_ATOP`/`XOR` are canvas-only. Keep canvas unless SVG in the page is asked for.
- SVG export from either renderer: `am5.renderToSVG(root)` (or an element, e.g. `series`) returns markup of the chart as last drawn — call it after `root.events.once("frameended", …)`; options `width`, `height`, `precision` (3), `idPrefix`, `title`, `background`. Exporting plugin: `exporting.download("svg")` / `getSVG()` / `exportSVG()`; `ExportingMenu` lists "SVG" by default (`svgOptions: { disabled: true }` removes it).
- `<am5-chart>` element: `<am5-chart themes="Animated" renderer="svg" config='{ "type": "PieChart", … }'>` (or `src="chart.json"`). Script tags: `index.js` > `plugins/json.js` > `element.js` > every chart package the config uses > themes. npm: `import "@amcharts/amcharts5/element"`, then `el.themes = [am5themes_Animated]; el.config = {…}`. `el.whenReady()` resolves `{ root, chart }`; events `ready`/`error`; 400 px high without a CSS height.
- `autoAppear: true` (+ `appearDuration`, `appearDelay`) on a chart/series plays the `appear()` animation when first drawn — the way to animate JSON configs. A series waits for its first data; plays once.
- `Root` `forcedColors` (default `true`), `Scrollbar` `outsideAxes` (`true` beyond the axes, `false` between axes and plot; only for `scrollbarX`/`scrollbarY`), `Modal` `ariaLabel`, element `ariaExpanded`.
- Maps: `am5map.PixelMapSeries` (polygons as a pixel grid: `pixelType` `"square"`/`"circle"`/`"diamond"`/`"hexagon"`, `step` (2°), `uniform`, `columnHeight` + `MapPolygon` `pixelHeight` via heat rule; style `mapPolygons.template`), `am5map.MapRasterSeries` (equirectangular world image `src`, optional `nightSrc` + `sunDate: "now"`), `am5map.NightSeries` (`sunDate`/`sunPosition`, `sunAltitude`), `am5map.getSunPosition(date)`, `MapLine` `altitude` (metres, one arc per leg), `MapPointSeries` `altitudeField` (no default) and `surfaceBullets`, `MapChart` `autoHome`, `MapPolygonSeries` `clickZoom` (click zooms to a polygon, again/background goes home; zoomed polygon is `active`). See references/map.md.
- JSON: colors from `root.interfaceColors` are written as `"@root.interfaceColors.get('…')"` references (follow the theme on parse); hidden series, plot/axis-container elements, data-item loops, `Date` values and more are now saved.

**Behavior changes (5.21.0):** a hidden element (`visible: false`/`forceHidden`/`hide()`) no longer takes space in a content-sized container (a hidden XY scrollbar leaves no band); `emptyAs` replaces only `null`/`undefined`/`""`; `Label` `fillOpacity: 0` hides text; `strokeWidth: 0` / `shadowOpacity: 0` draw nothing; heat rule `minValue: 0`/`maxValue: 0` honored; `stacked: "up"` bullets on vertical series stack; `calculateAggregates` change fields work on non-XY series; Gantt `colorField`/`nameField` honored; `Sunburst` ignores `singleBranchOnly`; `StockToolbar` `focusable` defaults to `true`; Responsive theme hides minor labels only at ≤ 600 px; `PatternSet` wraps past its last pattern; `DurationFormatter` codes `H`/`D`/`Y`/`K`/`k`/`n` work and month–year durations use month formats; `CSVParser` honors `skipEmpty: false`; `series.updateData([])` removes all items; `fontSize: "8"` = 8 px; a log `ValueAxis` with values ≤ 0 warns in the console (set `treatZeroAs`); `innerRadius: am5.percent(0)` works on pie/radar; `AxisRendererRadial` negative `radius` is measured in from the chart radius.

**New settings worth knowing:**

- New fill patterns `am5.StarPattern` and `am5.TrianglePattern` (5.20.0). `rotateShapes: true` on `RectanglePattern`/`StarPattern`/`TrianglePattern` rotates each shape around its own center instead of the whole grid — tiles seamlessly and is much faster.
- `XYChart`: `strokeWidths` and `strokeDasharrays` — arrays cycled across line series as they are added, like `colors`. Distinguish series without relying on color.
- `XYCursor`: `clickTolerance` (default `0`) — pixels outside the plot area where a zoom/select drag may start.
- `Series`: `fillGradient` / `strokeGradient`. Bullets with no paint of their own inherit fill/stroke/gradient/pattern from the series — or from their own slice/node on pie, funnel, flow and hierarchy charts.
- `XYSeries`: value fields (`valueYField`, …) can be changed after creation (re-set the data afterwards), and a series can be moved to a different `xAxis`/`yAxis`.
- `WordCloud` (5.20.1): `svgPath` arranges words into a shape, with `maskByShape` and `shapeTolerance`; `randomizeAngles: false` and `randomness: 0` give a reproducible layout; `allowNesting: false` packs non-overlapping bounding boxes (use with opaque label backgrounds). `angles` now accepts **any** angle (e.g. `[0, -30, -45]`) — the old `0`/`±90`-only restriction is gone.
- New `globalpointerdown` event on all elements (mirrors `globalpointermove`/`globalpointerup`).
- `Root`: `sanitizeHTML` (default `true`, 5.19.0) sanitizes dynamically-set HTML; exports gained `escapeFormulas` (default `true`) against CSV/XLSX formula injection.
- `MapChart`: `projectionName` string setting (5.19.0), e.g. `"geoOrthographic"` — mainly for JSON config; `am5map.registerProjection()` adds more.
- `Tree`: `fitNodes` (5.18.0), `nodeSeparation` / `clustered` (5.16.2). `Hierarchy`: `parentIdField` + `setFlatData()` (5.16.2). `ValueAxis`: `syncZeros` (5.16.2).
- All entities: `onDebounced(key, cb, delay)` / `offDebounced()` (5.17.3). `Label`: `fontFamily: "inherit"` (5.17.3).
- Stock indicators enforce min/max limits on numeric settings (5.20.0); `IIndicatorEditableSetting` gained `scale`, `maxValue`, `step`. Volume Profile now spreads volume across each bar's high/low range.
- `MapChart` (5.20.2): `doubleClickZoom` defaults to **true** (double click zooms in, shift + double click out — set `false` to opt out). `boxZoom: "none" | "drag" | "shift" | "ctrl" | "alt"` (default `"none"`, **not a boolean**) names the key held while dragging a zoom rectangle (`chart.boxZoomSelection`). No keyboard-navigation settings exist.
- `MapLineSeries` (5.20.3): `pointIds: ["JFK", "LAX"]` data field names the points a line connects, looked up in the `pointSeries` setting; `pointIdsField` renames the field. `pointsToConnect` wins if both are set.
- Column series (5.20.4): `colorByDataItem: true` colors each column from the series' `colors` (`ColorSet`) — prefer it over a `fill` adapter (adapters do not survive JSON serialization).
- `Scrollbar` (5.20.2): `opposite: true` puts `scrollbarX` below the plot / `scrollbarY` on the left. Different from the axis renderer's `opposite`.
- `Root` (5.20.2): `fontFamily`, `fontSize`, `fontWeight` settings — defaults for all text elements.
- `am5.SerialChartContainer` (5.20.2, `am5` root module): a `SerialChart` whose `seriesContainer` is a `ZoomableContainer` (`chart.zoomableContainer`), for zoomable/pannable `ForceDirected` etc.; optional `zoomTools` setting.
- All entities: `once(key, cb)` / `onceDebounced(key, cb, delay)` (5.20.4) — settings-change handler that fires once then removes itself.
- JSON (5.20.2–5.20.4): `ChartSerializer` emits **only user-set settings**; `includeRoot: true` writes a top-level `root` section (also accepted in hand-written configs); `parser.parse(config, { updateTargets: "soft" })` updates an existing same-type object instead of replacing it; Gantt is serializable; adapters that did not survive JSON are skipped on parse (they never round-trip).
- Bullets (5.20.2): flow node bullets are children of the node (above shape, below label), `ArcDiagram` node bullets sit on the node circle, funnel/pyramid bullets follow the slice's sloping edges. An unpainted bullet takes its **own slice/node color** on pie, funnel, flow and hierarchy charts — same color as what it sits on, so give it a contrasting `fill`/`stroke`.
- All elements: `animations` setting (5.20.8) — array of `{ key, from?, to, duration, delay?, loops?, yoyo?, easing?, ease?, target? }`: `loops: 0` = forever (default `1`), `easing` is a **name** (default `"linear"`), `ease: "in" | "out" | "inOut"` (default `"in"`), `target: "dataItem"` animates a data-item value such as `positionOnLine`. Declarative, so it lives in JSON configs. Give `from` explicitly unless the setting has a theme default (`scale`/`opacity`/`rotation`) — with `from` omitted and an `undefined` current value it jumps straight to `to`. E.g. a pulsing bullet: `am5.Circle.new(root, { radius: 6, animations: [{ key: "scale", from: 1, to: 1.6, duration: 800, loops: 0, yoyo: true, easing: "sine" }] })`.
- `am5.ease.byName("cubic", "out")` / `am5.ease.easingInfo(fn)` (5.20.8) — only `linear`, `quad`, `cubic`, `exp`, `sine`, `circle`, `bounce`, `elastic` (and `out`/`inOut`/`yoyo` of them) have names; unknown names become linear. `am5.ease.pow(t, e)` needs an exponent — wrap it as `(t) => am5.ease.pow(t, 3)`, never pass it bare.
- `Series` links (5.20.7): `urlField` (no default — off until set) + `linkTarget` (default `"_self"`; `"_blank"` opens with `noopener`). Clicking a bullet, column, slice (pie/funnel/pyramid/pictorial/Venn), map polygon or map line opens the data item's `url`; pointer cursor is automatic; `javascript:`/`data:`/`vbscript:` URLs are ignored; override `series.openUrl(dataItem)` to intercept. Not linked: hierarchy nodes, flow nodes/links, word-cloud labels, `MapSankeySeries` nodes.
- `MapPointSeries` (5.20.6): `lineIdField`, `positionOnLineField`, `autoRotateField`, `autoRotateAngleField` (defaults `"lineId"`, `"positionOnLine"`, `"autoRotate"`, `"autoRotateAngle"`) — points on lines can be data rows instead of `pushDataItem({ lineDataItem })`. An auto-rotating point turns round on the way back only while a bullet-sprite `animations` entry moves it (5.20.8).
- Fixes (5.20.6–5.20.7): series data no longer has to follow `CategoryAxis` category order (line series still connect in data order); log `ValueAxis` labels use round powers of ten; `axisHeader` content added later makes the axis leave room; `am5.CSVParser.parse("")` no longer hangs (returns `[]` with `useColumnNames: true`, `[{}]` by default); a `Container` `background` with its own `templateField` reads the container's data item (per-bullet label backgrounds work).
- JSON (5.20.6–5.20.8): user `themeTags` (passed to `.new()`) are serialized; `JsonParser` resolves refs that point further down the config (a legend in an `axisHeader` round-trips; axis-range `axis`/`series` lookups still need ordering); map data rows drop geodata properties (`name`, `CNTRY`, `TYPE`); declared `animations` round-trip and endless code-started loops with a named easing are saved as `animations` entries (`ChartSerializer` `runningAnimations`, default `true`). A loop started on a data item in code is saved only since 5.21.0.

## Verify unfamiliar API before using it

If unsure whether a method, property, or setting exists, **verify it** before using it:

1. **Primary:** `https://www.amcharts.com/docs/v5/reference/{classname}/` (lowercase, e.g. `LineSeries` > `lineseries`)
2. **Fallback:** TypeScript source on GitHub — `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amcharts/amcharts5/master/src/.internal/charts/` — settings interfaces are named `I{ClassName}Settings`

Common source paths:
- XY series: `charts/xy/series/{ClassName}.ts`
- XY axes: `charts/xy/axes/{ClassName}.ts`
- Pie: `charts/percent/pie/{ClassName}.ts`
- Radar: `charts/radar/{ClassName}.ts`
- Map: `charts/map/{ClassName}.ts`
- Core sprites: `core/render/{ClassName}.ts`

